From 25781be1cad87e887c2fe74deb3e864b002f0c5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 15:52:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v3.0.6: full backup carries /jffs; settings JSON embeds the
 .CFG; two panels, not four

Backup & Restore (owner-approved mockup 2026-09-03):
- .rbk gains a fourth part, the whole /jffs as a gzip tar (stock JFFS
  backup shape). Restore lists the tar before touching anything, then wipes
  and extracts /jffs as the stock JFFS restore did, stages the CFG and
  reboots; with the stores back as files no pending half is parked. An
  extraction failure after the wipe falls back to the pending path. Magic
  unchanged: older archives restore as before, older firmware ignores the
  new part. 96 MB cap on the part, 128 MB on the upload.
- reaper_cfg.cgi?action=export embeds the stock CFG as "cfg_b64" (same
  rbk_make_cfg generator). Same-model import rebuilds a .rbk in the browser
  (CFG + JSON) and sends it through reaper_restore.cgi; other model or
  older export strips it and runs the no-reboot JSON import as before.
- Reaper_Backup.asp: stock .CFG and JFFS cards removed, manifest pills on
  the two remaining cards, step 03 reworded to "only if prompted".
- Dicts: 9 keys reworded, RBKP_33-36 added, 24 languages translated,
  lockstep 6824. Stray untracked www/temp.dict removed.
